INSERT INTO player_matches VALUES(247,12,14025210,14,NULL,'2025-26','2025-12-14','West Ham United','A','PL',90,6.5,1,'RDM','pivot-centre',5,'4-2-3-1',42.29999999999999715,41.20000000000000285,59.5,91,'0,0,0,0,0,0,3,10,5,3,0,5,7,10,4,0,4,7,20,0,0,5,2,1,5','000000253203452024X003113',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'(match heatmap analysis)','QUALITATIVE READ. Deepest of the outfielders alongside Onana — hot zone is the central band just ahead of the CBs (Konsa/Lindelöf), forming the base that let Tielemans, McGinn and Rogers push on. Anchored the middle; positionally disciplined rather than a runner. MOVEMENT: minimal vertical roaming — stays central to screen and recycle. As West Ham (4-3-1-2) attacked centrally through Paquetá/Fernandes early, Kamara''s zone tightens centrally in the first half; in the dominant second half his average position edges higher as Villa camp in the WH half. Note: after Onana was subbed at 64'', Kamara covered more of the central pivot space alone alongside the incoming shape.','SofaScore API /event/14025210/average-positions (2026-07-02)','HIGH on avg coords (API). Minutes/rating not captured in this sweep; pos_class derived from coords alone. Collected to settle the pivot-side question; no appearances after 2026-01-10 (injury).');
